NIXL 1.5.1, UCX backend: register memory for reads alone on request.

NIXL's UCX backend maps every registration with UCX's default protection,
local and remote reads and writes (`ucp_mem_map` without
UCP_MEM_MAP_PARAM_FIELD_PROT). The verbs registration of a read-only mapping
refuses write access, so read-only host memory cannot be registered; with
UCX's non-blocking registration of host memory (UCX_REG_NONBLOCK_MEM_TYPES
includes `host` by default) the refusal is deferred to the first remote
read, which then never completes and reports no error.

With this patch a registration descriptor whose metadata (`metaInfo`, the
C API's `nixl_capi_reg_dlist_add_desc` metadata) is exactly `access=read`
is mapped with UCP_MEM_MAP_PROT_LOCAL_READ | UCP_MEM_MAP_PROT_REMOTE_READ:
the read-only mapping registers, and peers can READ it but not write it.
Every other registration keeps UCX's default. UniServe's Transfer Server
registers the read-only host storage it exposes to other hosts this way.

diff -ruN a/src/plugins/ucx/ucx_backend.cpp b/src/plugins/ucx/ucx_backend.cpp
--- a/src/plugins/ucx/ucx_backend.cpp	2026-10-28 05:59:37.313079345 +0000
+++ b/src/plugins/ucx/ucx_backend.cpp	2026-10-28 05:59:37.314079346 +0000
@@ -897,8 +897,14 @@
 {
     auto priv = std::make_unique<nixlUcxPrivateMetadata>();
 
+    // A descriptor whose metadata is "access=read" is registered for reads
+    // alone (local and remote): memory mapped read-only can be registered,
+    // and peers can only read it. Any other metadata keeps read and write
+    // access.
+    const bool read_only = mem.metaInfo == "access=read";
+
     // TODO: Add nixl_mem check?
-    const int ret = uc->memReg((void*) mem.addr, mem.len, priv->mem, nixl_mem);
+    const int ret = uc->memReg((void*) mem.addr, mem.len, priv->mem, nixl_mem, read_only);
     if (ret) {
         return NIXL_ERR_BACKEND;
     }
diff -ruN a/src/plugins/ucx/ucx_utils.cpp b/src/plugins/ucx/ucx_utils.cpp
--- a/src/plugins/ucx/ucx_utils.cpp	2026-10-28 05:59:37.312079344 +0000
+++ b/src/plugins/ucx/ucx_utils.cpp	2026-10-28 05:59:37.313079345 +0000
@@ -643,7 +643,11 @@
 
 
 int
-nixlUcxContext::memReg(void *addr, size_t size, nixlUcxMem &mem, nixl_mem_t nixl_mem_type) {
+nixlUcxContext::memReg(void *addr,
+                       size_t size,
+                       nixlUcxMem &mem,
+                       nixl_mem_t nixl_mem_type,
+                       bool read_only) {
     mem.base = addr;
     mem.size = size;
 
@@ -653,6 +657,14 @@
         .address = mem.base,
         .length = mem.size,
     };
+    /* Without a protection, UCX registers for local and remote reads and
+     * writes, which the verbs registration of a read-only mapping refuses
+     * (and a non-blocking registration then leaves every remote read of it
+     * unanswered). */
+    if (read_only) {
+        mem_params.field_mask |= UCP_MEM_MAP_PARAM_FIELD_PROT;
+        mem_params.prot = UCP_MEM_MAP_PROT_LOCAL_READ | UCP_MEM_MAP_PROT_REMOTE_READ;
+    }
 
     ucs_status_t status = ucp_mem_map(ctx.get(), &mem_params, &mem.memh);
     if (status != UCS_OK) {
